# --- ffmpeg/libav*: four more disclosed since the pass above
# (2026-08-28) -- found by re-running `trivy image` against a freshly
# built ttli-api on 2026-09-01. Checked security-tracker.debian.org
# directly for all three Debian tiers (bookworm, trixie, sid/unstable at
# 7:8.1.2-2): every one is still "vulnerable", waiting on the fix to
# land in ffmpeg's own 7.1.x branch first -- there is no newer Debian
# package to bump to, on any release. Also confirmed not reachable
# through this app's own use of ffmpeg regardless (services/media/
# pipeline.py, ffmpeg.py): source input is always a plain local path
# with no URL scheme (never rist://, never a DASH manifest fetch), and
# output is always `-f hls` fmp4 via libx264/aac (never MPEG-PS muxing,
# never VC-2/Dirac RTP) -- the four vulnerable code paths below are
# simply never invoked by build_ladder_args/run_transcode.
# CVE-2026-75142: stack buffer overflow, MPEG-PS muxer (mpegenc.c) -- not used, output is HLS/fMP4 only.
CVE-2026-75142 exp:2026-11-26
# CVE-2026-75143: heap buffer overflow, RIST protocol reader (librist.c) -- not used, input is never a rist:// URL.
CVE-2026-75143 exp:2026-11-26
# CVE-2026-75144: heap buffer overflow, VC-2/Dirac RTP packetizer (rtpenc_vc2hq.c) -- not used, no RTP output, no Dirac codec.
CVE-2026-75144 exp:2026-11-26
# CVE-2026-75146: OOB read, DASH demuxer on manifest refresh -- not used, input is a one-shot local file, never a live DASH manifest.
CVE-2026-75146 exp:2026-11-26

