# CVE-2026-87933 was first reported against the freshly built API image on
# 2026-09-15. Debian trixie ships libcjson1 1.7.18-3.1+deb13u1 and marks
# trixie, testing and sid vulnerable with no fixed package available. The
# bug is specifically in `cJSONUtils_MergePatch` from libcjson_utils.so,
# not cJSON's core parser. Debian packages that utils library together with
# libcjson.so, so package presence alone is not enough evidence to ignore it.
# The `images` job therefore grants this entry to ttli-api only and first
# performs a fail-closed binary sweep: any executable/shared object outside
# libcjson_utils.so that links `libcjson_utils.so` makes CI fail before Trivy.
# TTLI source contains no cJSON call site. Remove as soon as Debian publishes
# a fix; otherwise re-run the reachability guard and review at expiry.
CVE-2026-87933 exp:2026-12-14

